Z||000016||bcwawright||05-29-2001||10:30 PM||||Thanks for all the positive comments on the car. The headlights and hood are custom one-off that took about 4 months to design and construct,,,,, it was taken from the cover of Automobile magazine that introduced the F375 Ferrari. They do not in anyway resemble a Porsche. The BBS wheels are no longer produced they are 17x9 and 17x10. The stock frame was reinforced at the firewall area and the lenght of the console to the front tire area.....it has a gate short throw shifter that really works.....I am fixing to get rid of the wheel spacers and put a wide track suspension which will require lenghtening the drive shafts,,,,,,,,I will be putting up for sale the 88GT brakes and the complete rear suspension that has adjustable coil over shocks and I will be selling the 2" drop spindles with Held Motorsports A arms complete with coil over adjustable shocks.......If you are interested in any of theses parts you need to let me know now.....since they won't last long it will be whoever asks first. The wheels will also be forsale at a later date.<BR>When I completely finish the project it will handle and accelerate as good as any Ferrari.....Fieros Rule.<P>Bruce<P> ||||reg||6
Z||000017||bcwawright||05-29-2001||10:59 PM||||Pherder<BR>In my post I said "if possible". That did not mean that I wouldn't sell it seperately.......the interior is sooooo nice I just wanted to give the opporitunity to someone to buy it as a complete set.  Sorry you misunderstood what I was trying to say. Next time I have something forsale that you are interested in just email me and I will give you my phone number and I'll make sure you get first refusal.<BR>Thanks<P>Bruce||||reg||14
